  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 309 AM MDT TUE OCT 13 2026\nFriday through Saturday will continue to see dry conditions and\ntemperatures 5 to 10 degrees above normal as the large Pacific \nhigh continues to build in and amplify over the region. Clear \nskies and good radiational cooling overnight will allow for \nmountain valley fog development through the mornings. On Sunday,\na weak shortwave trough will pass over the northwest and bring \na dry cold front across our area. This frontal passage may bring\na slight cooldown Sunday through Monday. For now, temperatures \nare still looking to be 5 to 10 degrees above normal on those \ndays. Ensemble guidance remains in strong agreement on another \nclosed upper low digging into the region from the Gulf of Alaska\nlate Monday through midweek. Although slight uncertainty \nremains over the intensity and coverage, most areas should see \nsome moderate chances of precipitation late Monday through \nTuesday.",
